; Rear-plane bitmap: R0 has this pixel's coordinates in the buffers, which C0 turns into DS pixels: times C0.x and C0.y
; plus C0.z and C0.w gives them before rounding down. C1.x and C1.y add the clear image offset, and the images repeat
; every 256 pixels. The color image has each pixel's color and alpha, and the depth image has the DS depth and the fog
; flag. The attributes are the clear polygon ID times 4 in C1.z plus the fog flag, encoded by C2 and C3 like the
; polygons' are, with the depth limited to at least 1 for the log. The depth buffer gets the depth times C4.x, or with
; C1.w set for W-buffering, C4.y over it. Each instruction group has a single instruction, since groups can't read the
; same channel of different registers at once, which the assembler doesn't check.
00 ALU: ADDR(32) CNT(10)
    0  x: MULADD R4.x, R0.x, C0.x, C0.z
    1  y: MULADD R4.y, R0.y, C0.y, C0.w
    2  x: FLOOR R4.x, R4.x
    3  y: FLOOR R4.y, R4.y
    4  x: ADD R4.x, R4.x, C1.x
    5  y: ADD R4.y, R4.y, C1.y
    6  x: MUL R4.x, R4.x, (0x3B800000, 0.00390625f).x
    7  y: MUL R4.y, R4.y, (0x3B800000, 0.00390625f).x
01 TEX: ADDR(64) CNT(2) VALID_PIX
    8  SAMPLE R5, R4.xy00, t0, s0
    9  SAMPLE R6, R4.xy00, t1, s1
02 ALU: ADDR(42) CNT(13)
   10  x: MULADD R7.x, R6.y, 2.0f, C1.z
   11  x: MULADD R7.x, R7.x, C2.x, C2.y
   12  x: MAX R8.x, R6.x, 1.0f
   13  t: LOG_IEEE R8.y, R8.x
   14  y: MUL R8.y, R8.y, C2.w
   15  z: MUL R8.z, R6.x, C2.z
   16  y: CNDE R7.y, C3.x, R8.z, R8.y
   17  t: RECIP_IEEE R9.x, R8.x
   18  x: MUL R9.x, R9.x, C4.y
   19  z: MUL R9.z, R6.x, C4.x
   20  x: CNDE R10.x, C1.w, R9.z, R9.x
   21  x: MIN R10.x, R10.x, 1.0f
03 EXP: PIX0, R5
04 EXP: PIX1, R7
05 EXP_DONE: PIX61, R10
END_OF_PROGRAM
